ws3-z80-open-silicon-gf180mcu — component licensing
====================================================

Copyright (c) 2025-2026 Renaldas Zioma
Copyright (c) 2025 wafer.space project template contributors (AUTHORS.md)

Project: https://github.com/rejunity/ws3-z80-open-silicon-gf180mcu

This repository uses different licenses for different components. It is not
offered as a repository-wide choice between them.

1. The chip and its tooling — Apache-2.0

   Everything not named in sections 2 to 4 is licensed under the Apache
   License, Version 2.0 (LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt), as the wafer.space
   gf180mcu project template it derives from: the chip's top level and pad
   ring (src/chip_top.sv, src/chip_core.sv, src/slot_defines.svh), the
   LibreLane configuration (librelane/), the wafer.space IP views (ip/), the
   cocotb tests (cocotb/), scripts/, tests/run_zex.sh, the Makefile,
   .github/ and the documentation.

2. RZ80, the Z80 core — CERN-OHL-W-2.0

   src/rz80/ is the RTL of RZ80 (https://github.com/rejunity/z80-from-schematics,
   rtl/), copied unchanged by scripts/sync_rz80.py. It is licensed under the
   CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 — Weakly Reciprocal, SPDX identifier
   CERN-OHL-W-2.0 (LICENSES/CERN-OHL-W-2.0.txt), as each file's header says.
   HARDWARE_NOTICE.md carries its copyright and Source Location notices,
   including the section 4.1 requirement that Products made from it display
   the Source Location.

3. RZ80's test harnesses — MIT

   tests/rz80/ and timing/z8400_nmos.json are copies of RZ80's support
   software and data, written by scripts/sync_rz80.py (tests/rz80/README.md
   lists each file and its source). They keep RZ80's terms: the MIT License
   (LICENSES/MIT.txt), unless a file carries a different notice.

4. The rz80/ submodule and the test programs it holds

   rz80/ is a git submodule: RZ80 under its own LICENSE and
   THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. The tests read third-party programs and data from
   it rather than copying them here — Frank D. Cringle's ZEXDOC / ZEXALL and
   prelim (GPL-2.0-or-later), the FUSE tests (GPL), Patrik Rak's z80test
   (MIT), the BASIC ROMs, the sigrok KC 85/4 captures and perfectz80's
   recorded traces — and they keep their upstream licenses.

The license texts control. This file identifies their scope and does not
replace or modify their terms.
